e and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Speculating about Feelings and Impressions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you speculate about something, you are making a guess based on what you know about the situation.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can show you are speculating about something by using a modal, like <span class =\"italic\">must</span> or <span class =\"italic\">can't</span>.  The modal is followed by a verb.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The verb can be in the Present tense or the Present Perfect tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Psychologists must find this issue very intriguing, because many studies have been done on the subject.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "This can't be just a coincidence. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Conditional Sentences ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the First Conditional to say it's possible that you will do something. In that condition, something else may or will (not) happen.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "If you ask two people to remember an address, a person might try to picture the house and street.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "A different person may try to remember the sound of the spoken address if you ask the same question.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The sentence is divided into two clauses: the <span class =\"italic\">if</span> clause and the <span class =\"italic\">condition</span> clause.<br/><br/>The <span class=\"strong\">if</span>  clause can go at the start or the end of the sentence.  The <span class=\"strong\">if</span> clause is in the <span class=\"strong\">Present Tense</span>.  The condition clause is in the <span class=\"italic\">future</span> with <span class=\"strong\">will</span> or with the modal verbs <span class=\"strong\">might</span>, or  <span class=\"strong\">may</span> + the base form or the verb (the infinitive without \u2018to').", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">1st Clause</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">2nd Clause</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Meaning</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If you ask two people to remember an address, \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a person might try to picture the house and street.  \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's possible you ask two people to remember an address. In this condition: a person might try to picture the house and street.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A different person may try to remember the sound of the spoken address \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"if you ask the same question.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's possible you ask the question to somebody else. In this condition: a different person may try to remember the sound of the spoken address.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "intriguing", "type": "name"}, {"content": "makes you interested or curious", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Psychologists have found this issue so intriguing that many studies have been done on the subject.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you talk about the human senses.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sense", "type": "name"}, {"content": "means by which you obtain information about your environment (sight, hearing, touch, etc.)", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Most people relate to their surroundings through one main sense.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hearing", "type": "name"}, {"content": "ability to detect and understand sounds", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  The main senses are sight, hearing and touch. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "touch", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the ability to get information by placing your fingers on something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  You can get a lot of information through touch.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sight", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the ability to see things in your environment", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Not everyone relies on their sense of sight. Some people prefer to use their sense of hearing.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to picture", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to imagine", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: To remember an address, a person might try to picture the house and street.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sound", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a vibration that a person can detect and interpret", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A hearing-oriented person tries to remember the sound of the spoken address.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "smell", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the ability to get information about your environment from your nose", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The other senses are smell and taste. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob09aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "surroundings", "type": "name"}, {"content": "your immediate environment", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Most people relate to their surroundings through one main sense.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob09aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Talk to 10 people.  Explain the 5 senses.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask each person to identify which sense they use the most.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss why the person thinks this is the case.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Compile the results of the survey.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Design a graph, such as a bar graph, to show your results.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present your graph.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk to 10 people about  behavior and personality (human senses).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask questions about senses.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I design a graph to show the survey results.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present the survey.", "type": "text"}]}]}